{"content":"---\nname: project-defect-cocycle-csuite\ndescription: \"Collatz deterministic defect cocycle — C numerical suite build (Experiments A–I) + aipm provenance\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nBuilding the C numerical test suite specified in `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/collatz_defect_cocycle_c_specs.tex`, testing the defect cocycle W_{n,ℓ}(x;χ,s) of `defect_cocycle.tex`. Goal: is the finite spectral-shadow principle numerically plausible — NOT to prove Collatz. Critique read at `critiques/dc_1.md`.\n\n- **Code:** `deterministic_equidistribution_theory/c_suite/`, executable `collatz_tests`, 9 subcommands (A–I). ISO C11; `make` (FAST128 default), `make GMP=1`, `make DEBUG=1`; `make test` runs unit checks. Part of the `mynotes` git repo (not its own).\n- **aipm:** `.aipm/` initialized here (profile experimental-science, manuscript defect_cocycle.tex); claude-code capture hooks installed to project `.claude/settings.json`; added `**/*.c`,`**/*.h` to scan globs. Use installed `ailog` 0.1.0 (pipx, on PATH) — **lacks `prereg`/`graph`** (canonical repo f49bf3d has them; installed from 6f8a4ca). Pre-registrations logged via `ailog add`. Wrap builds/runs in `ailog run --`.\n\n**Critique-driven requirements baked in:** (1) Exp H mod-3^r congruence is a correctness GATE built first; (2) report rho_annealed and rho_exact as SEPARATE columns (never substitute annealed Fourier for exact operator); (3) shadow search flags limsup plateaus AND long sparse blocks, not just positive-density; (4) quenched pressure = limsup (1/n)Σ sΔ_b, not sum-over-words.\n\n**Progress:**\n- **M0 DONE+VERIFIED.** collatz_core/bigval (FAST128+GMP backends), orbit_scan (streaming, DEBUG invariants), modarith, io_csv (metadata headers), config, main. Exp H GATE PASSES: 226128/226128 (seeds 3–9999, r≤8, FAST128) + 144/144 GMP (seed 9999999999999999, r=12, deep n) → the mod-3^r sliding-window identity is numerically confirmed. Unit tests pass.\n- **M1 DONE+VALIDATED.** entropy_stats, critical_events (orbit recorder + excursions), Exp A (scan-height), Exp B (tilt-law). (A) height tail slope ≈ −1 ✓. (B) boundary-excluded middle bulk of high-ascent excursions leans to p^(1)=3·4^−b (KL_to_p1 < KL_to_annealed) ✓.\n- **M2/M3/M4 NOT STARTED:** characters+defect_sums (Exp C,D); residue_height_graph+sparse_matrix+spectral_tests (Exp E,F); trace_det (G) + shadow_search (I).\n\n**OPEN — needs user decision:** the \"C_A-critical\" definition is project-internal (H23a/PVT/SRCE, carried over without restatement). The spec's literal `V^2 ≤ 2^A P` floods event counts (every excursion once the orbit descends to small record-low V). Added `--crit-mode {vsq|height}`; `height` (peak ≥ launch·2^A) is the cleaner \"high ascent\" reading. Both show the Cramér-tilt direction in the middle bulk. Affects Exp B/D and the critical/high_ascent segment labels in C/I — confirm the formal certificate before finalizing those. Related to [[project-aipm]] dogfooding (installed CLI missing prereg/graph).\n","file_path":"/home/john/.claude/projects/-home-john-mynotes/memory/project_defect_cocycle_csuite.md"}